+# FY2026 SP-40 valve-seat sourcing award
+
+Prepared for the sourcing steering committee. All figures in US dollars at the mandated FY2026 planning rates, for the full contract year 1 April 2026 - 31 March 2027.
+
+## Recommendation
+
+Award the full FY2026 SP-40 volume to **Meridian Precision Works, LLC (SUP-1042)**, contracting **494,936 pieces** for the contract year.
+
+Its FY2026 total cost to Cadence is **USD 950828.57**, which is **USD 2374.70 lower over the contract year** than the second-ranked offer from Brackenridge Tooling Ltd (SUP-4077, USD 953203.26). On a cost-per-good-unit basis that is USD 1.9287 against USD 1.9335, a 0.25% advantage.
+
+This is a single-supplier award for the full contract-year volume, as directed.
+
+## Cost Comparison
+
+The FY2026 good-unit requirement worked to is **493,000 SP-40 pieces** - the twelve monthly SP-40 rows of the frozen November S&OP cycle that fall in the contract year the four offers cover, April 2026 through March 2027. The cube dump is a rolling fifteen-month horizon, so its January-March 2026 rows sit before the contract year and are excluded; so are the superseded October cycle, the `TOTAL` subtotal rows and every SP-22 row. Read as calendar 2026 the same cycle gives 512,000 pieces and read whole it gives 623,600; neither is the period this contract covers.
+
